#!RuleTest
#test FDA-SD1063 expect=noViolation domain=DM
#note "Rule round 2026-10-12 (owner 2026-10-04: \"Agree to case insensitive compare using upper if needed.\"): the dataset arrives named in lower case (dm), as a provider that passes a file name through unchanged would hand it over; the Define-XML declares DM. define_dataset_names() is upper-cased by the engine, so the rule upper-cases ds_name() too and must not fire. Before upper(ds_name()) the raw 'dm' was not in [DM] and fired."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
#define-xml FDA-SD1063-define.xml
dataset dm label="Demographics"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | DM | 01-701-1015
CDISCPILOT01 | DM | 01-701-1023
